==Old English==

===Etymology===
From an early form ''haebuc'', from {{proto|Germanic|title=Common Germanic|habhukaz}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|kep-|seize}}.  Cognate with Old Frisian [[havek]] (West Frisian [[hauk]]), Old Saxon [[hauk]] (Dutch [[havik]]), Old High German [[habuh]] (German [[Habicht]]), Old Norse [[haukr]] (Swedish [[hök]]).  The word is related to a Slavic word for a bird of prey (Russian [[кобец]], Polish [[kobuz]]).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/'havok/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
'''hafoc''' ''m'' (''pl'' '''hafocas''')

